.\Sonny's Desk
>.At Sonny's desk. There are Bloomberg screens in front of
>.him, a typical trading floor setup. There are other traders
..around him talking into the phone. 
>.Sonny is a good looking, well kept guy, who is using
>.profanity liberally. He works for SM (Shapley Morton), a
..large Wall Street brokerage firm. 
>.His associates Amisha and Joshua are sitting at their
>.respective desks. Joshua is trying to work on some
>.spreadsheets, but Amisha is just browsing her cell phone
>.with only the Outlook, the mail agent open on her two
..screens. 
>.Roger is from Hemispheric Energy, a gas and oil exploration
>.company. He is a typical non- Wall Street manager, overly
>.positive and exaggerating on everything he describes. Very
..shallow and vain. 
._Roger
>:So this is the business we came up
>:with - we have this really valuable
>:land, with lots of oil underneath.
>:Telling you man, they drilled there
>:already and, apart from some minor
>:hiccups, this thing looks
.:promising. 
._SONNY
>:OK, so how much are we talking
.:about.
._ROGER
>:Like, easily several millions
>:MMBtus, plus lots of oil, some can
.:be converted to jet fuel. 
>.Roger continues talking on the phone while Amisha comes
>.along and brings Sonny coffee. She is obviously flirty.
>.Sonny pushes her aside while holding the phone covered so
..that Roger can't hear them. 
._SONNY
.((to AMISHA)
>:Not now, Amisha. Leave it here
.:god-damit.
._ROGER
>((continues from where he
.(left over)
